If you admit all the people with 3+ ascensions, first/second best asc%
roles:
Bar (98): Val
Val (111): Wiz
Sam (76): Val
Kni (44): Bar
Ran (43): Val
Pri (35): Bar
Cav (51): Bar
Tou (42): Val
Arc (41): Val
Hea (37): Bar
Rog (42): Pri
Wiz (31): Val
Mon (37): Arc
Based on 426 players

Number in parens is total number of players for whom that was their
best role (whether or not they matched the 2nd-best role).

The numbers are super-flaky, though; e.g. the difference between Pri
and Val as a second-best for Rog is less than 2 players difference
(ties for 2nd best role were divided, so if my fav is Wiz and I'm tied
with Val and Sam that would count .5 each for Wiz: Val and Wiz:Sam).
And the preferences are tiny samples: a lot of players may be 1/5 in
one role and 1/4 in another and that'll count as a full point for the
latter even though you really can't say there's any measurable skill
difference.

You can try to control for that by throwing out roles that a player's
only ascended once, to increase the skill measure.

But if you only count roles that've been ascended at least twice (to
eliminate pure randomness), the numbers are pretty shady because
sample sizes of players are so small.  E.g. you wind up saying that
players who are best at wizards are 2nd-best at tourists, because of
the 11 players who have wizard as the favorite role you have 3 with
tou as the second favorite, including stats like:
http://alt.org/nethack/player-stats.php?player=Stabwound  It's really
a stretch to say there's anything definitive about what that player's
